From a2051f3e363cd3b1838c23f7091c98a0a76766bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Appana Durga Kedareswara Rao <appana.durga.rao@xilinx.com>
Date: Mon, 6 Jan 2025 22:44:47 -1200
Subject: [PATCH 082/110] net: axienet: Add support for 10G/25G MAC

Add support for 10G/25G MAC.
>From IP version 3.2, XXV Ethernet IP has a new GT reset status
register which provides information on whether TX and RX clock
is stable. There is a limitation in the IP where RX Block Lock
Status register cannot be read if GT RX recovered clock is not
ready. Hence this new register needs to be polled for GT reset
complete and then the Block Lock should be polled for link up.
This new register should be polled after GT reset is done and
before any other register access.

Signed-off-by: Appana Durga Kedareswara Rao <appana.durga.rao@xilinx.com>
Acked-by: Harini Katakam <harini.katakam@amd.com>
Signed-off-by: Suraj Gupta <suraj.gupta2@amd.com>
Reviewed-by: Radhey Shyam Pandey <radhey.shyam.pandey@amd.com>
State: not-upstreamable
Message-ID: <20250107104507.359136-10-suraj.gupta2@amd.com>
